{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-pair-graph-regime-trichotomy","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:pair-graph-regime-trichotomy","kind":"proposition","title":"Pair-graph regimes of $A$: $2\\bigl(\\binom A2-(3A-6)\\bigr)=(A-3)(A-4)$ splits $A\\ge2$ into $\\{2\\}$, $\\{3,4\\}$, $\\{\\ge5\\}$","tags":["regime","combinatorics","pair-graph","max-contact","no-fit"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.MassCore.PairGraphRegime.regime_trichotomy","text":"pair-graph-regime-trichotomy.md","leanSource":"pair-graph-regime-trichotomy.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:pair-graph-regime-trichotomy\"></a><p><em>For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\ge2</code> let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K_A</code> be the complete graph on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> vertices. Define the pair-graph regime of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> by</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">r(A)=\\begin{cases}\n\\mathrm{I} &#x26; \\binom A3 = 0,\\\\\n\\mathrm{II} &#x26; \\binom A3>0 \\text{ and } \\binom A2\\le 3A-6,\\\\\n\\mathrm{III} &#x26; \\binom A2 > 3A-6.\n\\end{cases}</code></pre>\n<p><em>Here <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\binom A3=0</code> says that <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K_A</code> has no triangle, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3A-6</code> is the number of edges of a triangulated 2-sphere on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> vertices. Then, for every natural number <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>,</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">2\\Bigl(\\tbinom A2-(3A-6)\\Bigr)=(A-3)(A-4),</code></pre>\n<p><em>and for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\ge2</code> exactly one of the following holds:</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><em><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A=2</code>, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r(A)=\\mathrm I</code>;</em></li>\n<li><em><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\in\\{3,4\\}</code>, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\binom A2 = 3A-6</code>, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r(A)=\\mathrm{II}</code>;</em></li>\n<li><em><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\ge5</code>, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\binom A2>3A-6</code>, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r(A)=\\mathrm{III}</code>.</em></li>\n</ol>\n<p><em>In particular the deltahedral max-contact count <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa(A)</code> (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa(2)=1</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa(A)=3A-6</code> for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\ge3</code>) equals <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\binom A2</code> if and only if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\le4</code>.</em></p>\n<p>The statement is integer arithmetic.</p>\n<p>Geometrically (classical, not used above): for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\ge3</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\binom A2\\le3A-6</code> says <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K_A</code> is the 1-skeleton of a triangulated 2-sphere (the doubled triangle at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A=3</code>, the tetrahedron at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A=4</code>); for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\ge5</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K_A\\supseteq K_5</code> is not planar. Equivalently, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> equal spheres in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{R}^3</code> can be pairwise tangent if and only if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A\\le4</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pair-graph-regime-trichotomy.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.34.5","page":"b/prop-pair-graph-regime-trichotomy","qa":{"counts":{"pass":1,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":0,"unknown":0,"stale":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassCore.PairGraphRegime.regime_trichotomy","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pair-graph-regime-trichotomy.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
